@title Several pages in the navigator: Ctrl and Shift click, drag them as a block
@area Schematic
@sizes 1920x1080
# Ctrl+click adds a page to the selection or takes it out, Shift+click selects the range from the last click, and dragging one selected page drags them all: a badge shows the count and a line shows where the block lands. The outline is pinned at this size, so this scenario is 1920x1080 only. The pictures are the evidence: Ctrl selection, Shift range, mid-drag with the drop line, and the new order.
click_text "Open example"
wait 20
click 124 213
wait 6
click 150 358 ctrl
wait 6
click 150 416 ctrl
wait 6
shot ctrl-selected-10-and-30
click 100 358
wait 4
click 100 416 shift
wait 6
shot shift-range-10-to-30
mouse_down 120 387
move 120 400
move 120 420
move 120 440
move 120 452
wait 6
shot dragging-block-with-drop-line
mouse_up 120 452
wait 10
shot block-moved-below-40
key ctrl+z
wait 10
shot undone-in-one-step
key ctrl+a
wait 6
shot ctrl-a-all-pages
key Escape
wait 6
shot escape-clears
check_layout
